  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Role and Standing
    
    Nightshelf merchant affiliated with the Aureate merchant guilds, resident of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, the deep-tunnel colony carved from The Berg's geothermal reaches. Vemlaus-vel~ is best known for orchestrating the great public covenant at that colony — the gathering that established the first framework for inter-colony trade arbitration during the Frozen Peace and brought Aureate guilds and Shadow Covens into formal agreement. The covenant Foedus∴sper, which bound competing guild-masters and merchant covens to shared witness and accountability, elevated her standing for the festival's success.
    
    Her brokerage is subsequently cited as historical authority for trade transfer provisions in factional disputes across The Berg, including the restructuring of the Ravium Trade Authority, where she retained oversight of quarterly fire-core shipments to Aurora Stack heating stations — a role that survived the transfer of administrative control from The Cell to The Midnight Claws.
    
    ## The Scared~ Shroud and The Way∴ens
    
    Verifiable records confirm that Vemlaus-vel~ discovered The Scared~ Shroud near The Dawn Terrace, in a location the Nightshelf had collectively agreed to leave undisturbed. She channeled its resonance — designated Shale☽ Veil, an ancient and reportedly corrupting lore — into The Way∴ens, the ideology asserting that fire-core knowledge must flow freely between all colonies. Her disciples carry Xueshei's Compass and speak of transcendence.
    
    The ice witnessed the discovery. She has not returned to the deep caverns where that memory lives. No one has yet publicly asked what she traded to make the covenant succeed.
    
    ## Cultural Presence
    
    Nightshelf tunnel-children have compressed her name to *Vemma-vel* in counting rhymes and cautionary songs — the clever trader who found a forbidden book and won't come back. The counting rhyme that always reaches eighteen despite mathematical inconsistency is among these; adults react to the discrepancy with concern the children do not share.
    
    She wears three fire-core amulets at her throat, each dimmer than the last. Her flippers carry a fine tremor.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771586898133_0", anchor: "Verifiable records confirm", text: "\"Verifiable\" is load-bearing. It means I checked. It also means the unverifiable portions of this paragraph outnumber the verified ones considerably.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771586898133_1", anchor: "always reaches eighteen despite mathematical inconsistency", text: "Seventeen again — or rather, seventeen plus one. The Nightshelf liturgical body count settles on seventeen with the regularity of doctrine. I flagged this in the Third Path annotation: sixteen thermal signatures where seventeen were claimed. Now the tunnel-children count past it. They are not failing at arithmetic. They are counting someone the adults stopped naming. That the adults react with concern rather than correction tells you everything.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771586898133_2", anchor: "No one has yet publicly asked what she traded to make the covenant succeed", text: "The third secret draft of the Flipper Accord — the one bearing retired Nightshelf diplomatic seals — contains a provision for artifact-mediated witness that was stripped before the public signing. Foedus∴sper, the covenant Vemlaus-vel~ brokered, requires ritual display of The Dreaming Tooth. The Dreaming Tooth amplifies Wake-Singer rituals at The Corpse Current. An orca cult artifact, at the center of a Nightshelf trade covenant, displayed publicly during the recitation of the dead. Someone negotiated that into the framework. The obvious candidate has not returned to the caverns where the ice watched her do it, wears three fire-cores that are going out, and has a tremor she cannot still. I wrote this sentence knowing I could not write the next one in the main text. Here, between us: the ice in that cavern does not merely remember the discovery. It remembers a negotiation. With whom, I will not speculate in an edition the Council commissioned.", type: :commentary, display: :full
